#. Tag: title
#: man-kjscmd5.1.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "Utilización"

#. Tag: para
#: man-kjscmd5.1.docbook:92
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The most common way to run <command>kjscmd</command> is simply as "
#| "<literallayout>\n"
#| "<userinput><command>kjscmd</command> <parameter>file</parameter>\n"
#| "</userinput>\n"
#| "</literallayout> If no parameter <parameter>file</parameter> is used, it "
#| "executes a predefined test script that measures the start speed of "
#| "<command>kjscmd</command>."
msgid ""
"The most common way to run <command>kjscmd5</command> is simply as "
"<literallayout>\n"
"<userinput><command>kjscmd5</command> <parameter>file</parameter>\n"
"</userinput>\n"
"</literallayout> If no parameter <parameter>file</parameter> is used, it "
"executes a predefined test script that measures the start speed of "
"<command>kjscmd5</command>."
msgstr ""
"O xeito máis habitual de executar <command>kjscmd</command> é como "
"<literallayout>\n"
"<userinput><command>kjscmd</command> <parameter>ficheiro</parameter>\n"
"</userinput>\n"
"</literallayout> De non usar o parámetro <parameter>ficheiro</parameter>, "
"executa un script predefinido de probas que mide a velocidade de arranque de "
"<command>kjscmd</command>."

